## Limits and next acceptance

This is not a complete SQL parser or universal dialect guarantee. Nested
queries keep PostgreSQL's native resolution, including explicitly qualified
correlated references; SQLite-specific unqualified outer references in a
subquery are not separately qualified by this repair and may still fail
loudly as ambiguous. The tested local query scopes are qualified only as
listed above. MySQL syntax acceptance, arbitrary capacity and existing-table
migrations remain unqualified. The prior finite-width/nondefault MySQL format
limits stand unchanged.

PGlite is local PostgreSQL execution; D1 is a local fixture runtime; Hrana
backends use local protocol mocks. Native MySQL, Bun and hosted providers were
not installed or run. No hosted/cloud/VM request, production reload or live
database write occurred. No new binaries, dependency install, server or
private data were needed. Test-owned scratch is cleaned by its existing
fixture teardown; raw run receipts and these deliverables remain retained.

